{# ONE PROPERTY PILL — grammar 3's peer property, and with `prominent` set,
   grammar 3a's lead. Lifted out of `form`'s own `pill()` macro unchanged.

   WHY IT IS ITS OWN COMPONENT NOW. `form` composes its regions from RENDERED
   content: a field widget renders itself and the surface places it. A macro is
   not addressable from outside the file that declares it, and both a widget and
   a scene have to be able to render exactly this pill, so the macro became a
   component. Nothing about the markup moved.

   THE PANEL IS COMPOSED HERE FROM PLAIN OPTION DATA and never handed in as
   rendered content, which is what lets a caller state a pill as a handful of
   strings and a list of `{value, label, selected}`.

   THE FIELD LIST IS THE UNION OF TWO CONTRACTS, and this is the one place that
   union is spelled. `clearable`, `clear_label`, `creatable` and `create_label`
   belong to `option_list`, because a clear row and a create row ARE rows of the
   listbox; `icon`, the value labels and the search box sit on the trigger and
   belong to `option_picker`. Each field goes to whichever of the two owns it,
   which is the same rule the picker cell in `table.twig` follows — and it is why
   a caller never has to know the split.

   AN OMITTED PROP IS DROPPED, NOT PASSED AS NULL, and that is a rendering
   requirement rather than tidiness. Neither `clear_label` nor `create_label` is
   required by `option_list.component.yml`, but both are declared `type: string`,
   and SDC's prop validation rejects an explicit NULL for a typed property where
   it accepts an absent key — measured as
   `[bb_theme:option_list/clear_label] NULL value found, but a string ... is
   required` the first time this surface was rendered anywhere validation is
   enabled. Validation is OFF on a stock site and ON under `KernelTestBase`, so
   the macro this replaces carried the same defect and never showed it; the rule
   used to live in a private method of `BbTicketCreateForm`, which filtered
   NULLs out by hand, and it belongs here now with the split it is part of.
   `|filter` and not a hand-written key list, so a prop added later is covered by
   the same line.

   THE ACCESSIBLE NAME IS LEFT TO `option_picker` when the caller passes none.
   That component already derives the state-carrying sentence from the field name
   and the value, so deriving it a second time here would be a second spelling of
   one name that could disagree with the first. A caller passes `aria_label` where
   the derived sentence would not agree in number — "no labels ARE set" against
   "no conductor IS set" — which is a property of English and not of the grammar.

   `attributes` IS FORWARDED RATHER THAN WRAPPED. This component adds no node of
   its own: a pill is the picker, and a wrapper here would sit between the lead
   row or the property row and the flex child it lays out. The single root this
   component has is `option_picker`'s, so the caller's attributes go there. #}
{%- set panel_props = {
  multiple: multiple|default(false),
  options: options|default([]),
  clearable: clearable|default(false),
  clear_label: clear_label,
  creatable: creatable|default(false),
  create_label: create_label,
}|filter(value => value is not null) -%}
{%- set panel %}
  {{- include('bb_theme:option_list', panel_props, with_context = false) -}}
{% endset -%}
{%- set picker_props = {
  variant: 'field',
  label: label,
  name: name,
  id: picker_id,
  prominent: prominent|default(false),
  icon: icon,
  multiple: multiple|default(false),
  searchable: searchable|default(false),
  selected_chips: selected_chips|default(false),
  selected: selected|default([]),
  search_placeholder: search_placeholder,
  search_label: search_label,
  search_url: search_url,
  aria_label: aria_label,
  value_label: value_label,
  value_labels: value_labels,
  values: values|default([]),
  open: open|default(false),
}|filter(value => value is not null) -%}
{{ include('bb_theme:option_picker', picker_props|merge({
  options: panel,
  attributes: attributes ?: create_attribute(),
}), with_context = false) }}
{#- WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT the panel never opens, so `fallback` adds the same rows as real form controls
    under the field's own name. They follow the picker's hidden inputs in the document, so a choice
    made here is the value the form submits. #}
{%- if fallback and name %}
<noscript>
  {{- include('bb_theme:option_list', panel_props|merge({
    input_name: name,
    input_type: multiple|default(false) ? 'checkbox' : 'radio',
  }), with_context = false) -}}
</noscript>
{%- endif %}
